  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Harshal Vijaykumar Patni vs The Commuissioner And Another on 21 June, 2024 2024:Bhc-Aug:11621 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 772 Of 2024 Harshal S/O Vijaykumar Patil Versus The Commissioner Of Police And Another Mr. Mohd. Aseem Mohd. A. K., Advocate for the applicant Mrs. K. R. Jamdhade, App for the respondent/State And Anticipatory Bail Application No. 733 Of 2024 Vijay Babasaheb Lambhe Versus The Commissioner Of Police And Another Mr. A. R. Borulkar, Advocate for the applicant Mrs. K. R. Jamdhade, App for the respondent/State Coram : R. M. Joshi, J. Date : 21st June, 2024 Per Court :- 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "It is the contention of the learned counsel for the applicants that the name of the applicants does not appear in the first information report to be the persons from whose custody the contraband articles are seized. 3. Learned APP opposed the application by contending that during the course of the investigation name of the applicants have revealed as supplier of the contraband articles and hence, they are not entitled for anticipatory bail. Learned APP informed the Court that the present applicants are found involved in similar crime earlier and they are enlarged on bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is the contention of the learned counsel for the applicants that the name of the applicants does not appear in the first information report to be the persons from whose custody the contraband articles are seized. 3. Learned APP opposed the application by contending that during the course of the investigation name of the applicants have revealed as supplier of the contraband articles and hence, they are not entitled for anticipatory bail.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned APP informed the Court that the present applicants are found involved in similar crime earlier and they are enlarged on bail.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
